      "created_at": "2014-04-02T19:37:17.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Back in the days when the year was better-suited to make novelty glasses out of, when Flash was young and the internet was alive with animators making movies of all kinds, there was one animation-making site which rose high above the seas of mediocrity. Its name... was <a href=\"http://www.homestarrunner.com/firsttime.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Homestarrunner.com</a>.</p><p>Featuring a host of bizzarre characters, highly quotable writing, witty satire, and a strange but unique style of humor, this family-friendly site produced top-quality shorts for a whole decade. At the height of its popularity, it got an original song into Rockband, created an actual band based off a fake band in the show, and even produced a series of video games for the Wii. But then, the updates gradually got less and less frequent, until they stopped altogether in December of 2010.</p><p>Well, it just <a href=\"http://www.homestarrunner.com/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">updated</a> on April 1st. What do you think it means? Is this a sign there are more to come, or was it just a one-off April Fool's joke? What future hairstyles can we expect next?</p>",
